    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="d329-4" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve10/pgd329-4"/>

                <head>330. Telegram 729 From the Embassy in Guatemala to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d330-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d330-f2"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Guatemala City</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1970-06-06T21:03:00+00:00">March 6,
                            1970, 2103Z</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <pb facs="d330-1" n="1" xml:id="pgd330-1"/>
                <p>1. Have just confirmed that Sean Holly, Labor Officer, kidnapped approximately
                    1430 by 4 armed masked men in zone 4. His car found abandoned with his jacket
                    and identity papers.</p>
                <p>2. Further details as available.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d330-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 785,
                    Country Files, Latin America, Guatemala, Vol. I. Confidential; Critic; Limited
                    Official Use. In telegram 746 from Guatemala City, March 7, the Embassy
                    forwarded a transcript of a FAR bulletin in which the guerrillas claimed
                    responsibility for Holly’s kidnapping and threatened to execute him if the
                    Guatemalan Government failed to release four imprisoned FAR guerrillas. (Ibid.,
                    RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, POL 23–8 GUAT)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d330-f2" n="2" xml:id="d330-f2-content">
                <p>The Embassy reported that Labor Officer Sean Holly had been kidnapped.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
